WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.211
[MUSIC]

00:00:02.211 --> 00:00:03.820
My name is Dan Miller.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:04.881
I am the founder and

00:00:04.881 --> 00:00:06.780
CEO of Spora Health.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.807
We are a primary care practice

00:00:08.807 --> 00:00:10.348
uniquely designed for

00:00:10.348 --> 00:00:11.569
people of color.

00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:13.401
I've had hundreds of meetings from

00:00:13.401 --> 00:00:15.112
Fortune 100 companies down to

00:00:15.112 --> 00:00:16.240
startups.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.669
I'm often the only person of color

00:00:18.669 --> 00:00:20.929
in the room trying to get folks to

00:00:20.929 --> 00:00:23.442
understand the experience of black

00:00:23.442 --> 00:00:24.866
and brown people and

00:00:24.866 --> 00:00:27.211
how they relate to healthcare and

00:00:27.211 --> 00:00:30.310
the issues that are impacting them.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.523
It's increasingly important for

00:00:32.523 --> 00:00:34.582
more representation not just in

00:00:34.582 --> 00:00:36.795
senior leadership across tech and

00:00:36.795 --> 00:00:37.634
business but

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.780
especially in healthcare.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.841
If we don't meet those expectations

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.960
then people don't get access.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.222
Those things motivate me to create

00:00:46.222 --> 00:00:48.641
more impacts professionally to help

00:00:48.641 --> 00:00:50.826
more folks to think thoughtfully

00:00:50.826 --> 00:00:52.621
about what representation

00:00:52.621 --> 00:00:54.814
really means and why it matters.

00:00:54.814 --> 00:00:56.031
As an entrepreneur,

00:00:56.031 --> 00:00:57.456
I don't have much time.

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:59.511
I needed to find a way for me

00:00:59.511 --> 00:01:02.221
to upskill myself but also learn in

00:01:02.221 --> 00:01:04.933
an incredible environment to make

00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:07.363
sure that I am building the best

00:01:07.363 --> 00:01:10.840
business and the best culture.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.931
I was very confident in my skills

00:01:13.931 --> 00:01:16.792
to go from zero to one but going

00:01:16.792 --> 00:01:19.890
from one to N was very new for me.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.468
There are incredible professors

00:01:22.468 --> 00:01:25.229
here and other classmates that have

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:27.807
thought about these problems and

00:01:27.807 --> 00:01:29.570
challenges in depth.

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:31.810
And there's a lot of research and

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:34.050
support that SEP and Stanford can

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.290
offer entrepreneurs to help them

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.858
progress throughout their careers.

00:01:38.858 --> 00:01:41.121
It's been an incredible experience

00:01:41.121 --> 00:01:42.581
to learn from folks that

00:01:42.581 --> 00:01:44.552
have thought a lot about not just

00:01:44.552 --> 00:01:46.888
growing business, not just creating

00:01:46.888 --> 00:01:48.713
innovative environments but

00:01:48.713 --> 00:01:50.759
also leaving a positive impact.

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:53.478
With this focus on making the world

00:01:53.478 --> 00:01:55.447
a more positive place and

00:01:55.447 --> 00:01:57.333
more equitable place.

00:01:57.333 --> 00:02:04.295
[MUSIC]

